                    "url": "https://www.cagbc.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Green-Retrofit-Economy-Study.pdf",
                    "title": "Green Retrofit Economy Study",
                    "content": "In order to catalyze a self-sustaining local green retrofit economy that facilitates investment and mobilizes capital towards large portfolios of building retrofit projects, several enabling conditions need to be in place, including: ༝ Adequate local workforce capacity to meet the labour demand CAPACITY POLICY ༝ Skills and training partnerships to equip the modern green building workforce with the knowledge required ༝ Access to high performance building materials in the local supply chain & TRAINING CAPITAL ༝ Strategies for securing available capital financing ༝ Supportive policy at all levels of government that provide a clear roadmap upon which investments in training and retrofit projects can be secured Green Retroﬁt Economy LABOUR EDUCATION, SKILLS PRODUCTS & EQUIPMENT AVAILABLE SUPPORTIVE GREEN RETROFIT ECONOMY STUDY | 9 Drawing from the recent Decarbonizing Canada’s Large Buildings study by CaGBC, considerations to help create the conditions to ramp up retrofit market activity and optimize deep carbon retrofits include: ༝ Aligning capital planning and regular infrastructure and equipment renewal timelines with green retrofit opportunities ༝ Supporting building owners to develop a strategy for securing capital financing for retrofit projects ༝ Leveraging an integrated design process approach to retrofit project development, moving away from single system improvements, and including an assessment of opportunities to maximize additional building perfor­ mance and occupant health benefits ༝ Starting as soon as possible, through the implementation of proven emissions reduction and efficiency measures and development of zero carbon transition plans.",
